  "notes": "USAGE:\nA somewhat literary word that implies deep, prolonged thinking. Often appears in set phrases.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {思案|しあん}に{暮|く}れる (to be lost in thought)\n- {思案|しあん}の{末|すえ} (after much deliberation)\n- {思案|しあん}{投|な}げ{首|くび} (racking one's brains; lit. \"thought-throwing neck\")\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {熟考|じゅっこう}: careful consideration — more formal, emphasizes thoroughness\n- {検討|けんとう}: examination, review — more practical and systematic, common in business",
